2026-11-11T11:39:57.3345987Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3346343Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3346769Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3347617Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3348066Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3348407Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3349129Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3349775Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3350467Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3351119Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3352305Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3353074Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3353914Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3354308Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3354742Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3355460Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3356132Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3356749Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3357046Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3357413Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3357772Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3358111Z Run one block of tests/features.py, from a marker line to the next block.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3358505Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3358915Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... "<first line of the block>" [END]
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3359847Z     python3 tools/audit/seat/features_block.py [--prelude 'import line']... --through "<marker line>"
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3360315Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3360693Z features.py runs every block in one process, which takes tens of minutes on a
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3361587Z loaded seat; a mutation proof needs only the block that pins the mutated line.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3362601Z The block is the text from the line containing START up to END (default: the
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3363279Z script's closing ``sys.exit``), executed in the namespace features.py's own
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3364285Z header builds -- ``R``, ``Coord``, the harness fakes -- with ``__file__``
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3365089Z pointing at features.py, so path arithmetic inside the block resolves as in
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3365775Z the full run. Exit status is the block's ``R.close``: 0 when every check passed.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3366323Z Run from the repository root under the CI venv.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3366580Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3366920Z ``--prelude`` (repeatable) runs one line, typically an import an earlier block
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3367593Z made, before the block. ``--through MARKER`` takes no block: it runs the whole
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3368284Z script from the top up to the line holding MARKER, the state every earlier
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3368869Z block builds, and exits with that prefix's ``R.close``.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3369159Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3369495Z ``--self-test`` runs offline: it executes a two-check block it writes itself.
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3369850Z 
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3370175Z   ok   _main: --through with a block, or no argument, is a usage error, rc 2
2026-11-11T11:39:57.3371156Z   ok   --through reports the prefix's own failure (null control)
